{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.StandardModel.LeptonNumberGradingObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.StandardModel.LeptonNumberGradingObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Subgroup.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Submodule.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.lepton_number_would_be_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.lepton_number_would_be_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/LeptonNumberGradingObstruction.lean#L133-L151","doc":"**Consequence: the grading would make lepton number identically zero.**\n\nLepton number is supposed to count smoothings, so a state with `L = k > 0`\nis represented by a nonzero grade-`k` class.  But if the skein relation holds\nat every crossing — which it does, it is the defining relation of the Skein\nmodule — then every smoothing term is `0` by `skein_forces_vanishing`.\n\nFormally: if every grade-`(g+1)` element arises as a skein term of grade-`g`\ncrossings, the whole positive-degree part collapses, so the grading cannot\ndistinguish a lepton-carrying state from a nuclear one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.skein_grading_kills_smoothing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.skein_grading_kills_smoothing","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/LeptonNumberGradingObstruction.lean#L119-L131","doc":"With the skein coefficient exhibited: the smoothing term\n`(q - q⁻¹) • L₀` is annihilated by the grading.\n\nStated over a generic commutative ring acting on `M`; scalars are\ngrade-preserving, so `c • L0` lies in the same component as `L0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.SmoothingGrading.skein_forces_vanishing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.SmoothingGrading.skein_forces_vanishing","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/LeptonNumberGradingObstruction.lean#L96-L115","doc":"**The obstruction.**\n\nIf the two crossing classes `Lp`, `Lm` are homogeneous of grade `g` and the\nskein term `S` is homogeneous of grade `g + 1`, then the skein relation\n`Lp - Lm = S` forces **both** sides to vanish: `S = 0` and `Lp = Lm`.\n\nThe skein relation is inhomogeneous, so it cannot hold in a graded module\nunless it is trivial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.SmoothingGrading.independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.SmoothingGrading.independent","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/LeptonNumberGradingObstruction.lean#L90-L90","doc":"Distinct graded components meet only in `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.SmoothingGrading.piece","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.SmoothingGrading.piece","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/LeptonNumberGradingObstruction.lean#L88-L88","doc":"The grade-`g` component: classes represented by diagrams with exactly\n`g` smoothings applied. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.SmoothingGrading.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.SmoothingGrading.mk","kind":"ctor","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/LeptonNumberGradingObstruction.lean#L85-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.SmoothingGrading","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.SmoothingGrading","kind":"structure","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/LeptonNumberGradingObstruction.lean#L77-L90","doc":"The data the `.md` claims: a `ℤ`-indexed family of homogeneous\ncomponents of the Skein module, indexed by smoothing count.\n\n`independent` is the defining property of a grading that we use: an element\nlying in two *distinct* components is zero.  (This is strictly weaker than a\nfull internal direct-sum decomposition, so the obstruction below is\ncorrespondingly strong — it does not need the full `DirectSum` structure to\nbite.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}